    "q3_reduce_required_splits": "At 75% budget, best adaptive (entropy_priority) macro F1=0.566 vs baseline 100% F1=0.597 (25% fewer splits). **Partially** \u2014 25% split reduction costs 0.031 macro F1; priority allocation improves partial-budget efficiency but does not fully replace the full rho=0.90 split tree.",
    "q4_refinement_allocation": "Compared to BFS rho at equal split budgets, priority scheduling improves macro F1 by +0.0297 at 50% and +0.0000 at 100%. Branch replay diagnostics showed ordering matters under partial budgets; this experiment confirms that **refinement allocation (scheduling) is a real missing component** beyond purity stopping and ball-count budgets. Impurity/boundary-weighted scheduling concentrates early splits on high-entropy regions, improving limited-budget granulation."
